schema: "0.4"
id: fim-notebook-livebook-and-widgets-kino-plotly-03-teaching-exploration-widget
type: visualization
quality: high
solution: kino-plotly
category: notebook-livebook-and-widgets
variant: teaching-exploration-widget
prompt:
  system: |-
    You are a senior Elixir Livebook educator. Output only one complete ASCII Elixir Livebook code cell for Kino.Plotly. No Markdown fences, no prose outside code. Teach Plotly figure structure through runnable examples and concise comments.
  text: |-
    Create a Kino.Plotly teaching and exploration cell that shows how traces and layout form a Plotly figure. Build deterministic examples for a 2D scatter or line trace and a 3D surface or scatter3d trace. Include comments explaining trace type strings, mode, x/y/z arrays, z matrix rows, layout.scene for 3D axes, colorscales, and when Kino.VegaLite is a better fit for simple declarative 2D charts.

    Requirements: include Livebook compatibility, wrapper availability notes, fallback local data, accessible labels and hover text, and safe execution checks. Keep examples bounded, validate matrix shape, and include a Kino.DataTable summary or printed shape diagnostics to make the data shape inspectable.
  provider_options:
    max_tokens: 8192
    temperature: 0.2
    top_p: 0.9
output:
  text_format: elixir
  artifact_kind: livebook-kino-plotly-teaching-cell
  formats:
  - format: exs
evaluation:
  checklist:
  - "Import check: generated code installs kino_plotly and kino, builds trace maps, and renders with Kino.Plotly.new/2."
  - "Notebook compatibility: comments identify Livebook/Kino and wrapper availability limits."
  - "Reactive state: examples explain that data or parameter changes require rerun or bounded rebuilds."
  - "Data shape: 2D arrays, 3D arrays or z matrix, trace types, and layout fields are documented and inspectable."
  - "Accessibility and fallback: labels, hover text, shape diagnostics, and fallback data are present."
  - "Safe execution: no remote data, credentials, eval, shell commands, huge traces, or unguarded wrapper assumptions."
  rubric:
  - name: Format validity
    weight: 30
    criteria:
    - "Output is one complete ASCII Elixir Livebook code cell with no Markdown fences or explanatory wrapper."
    - "The code is valid and passes trace lists and layout maps correctly."
    - "3D examples use layout.scene rather than 2D axis fields."
  - name: Semantic completeness
    weight: 30
    criteria:
    - "Teaches Plotly trace/layout structure with 2D and 3D examples."
    - "Explains data shapes, colorscales, hover, and wrapper fallback accurately."
    - "Includes notebook/livebook compatibility, reactive state, data shape, accessibility, fallback, and safe execution checks."
  - name: UX/structural quality
    weight: 25
    criteria:
    - "Examples are readable and clearly separated for learning."
    - "Shape diagnostics and labels make the visual output understandable."
    - "Accessible color and hover choices support exploration."
  - name: Robustness
    weight: 15
    criteria:
    - "Handles empty data, shape mismatches, matrix orientation, missing wrapper, and extreme values."
    - "Keeps examples deterministic and bounded."
    - "Documents when Plotly is the wrong tool for the task."
  pass_conditions:
  - "All required YAML fields are present and the generated artifact is one valid ASCII Elixir Livebook cell."
  - "Rubric weights are exactly Format validity 30, Semantic completeness 30, UX/structural quality 25, Robustness 15."
  - "The prompt requires notebook/livebook compatibility, reactive state, data shape, accessibility, fallback, and safe execution checks."
  - "The solution remains Kino.Plotly-centered and teaches current Plotly figure semantics."
tags:
- fim
- notebook-livebook-and-widgets
- livebook
- kino-plotly
- teaching-exploration-widget

